Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:43:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] feat(frontend): route-level code splitting with
 Suspense and error boundaries

Every page in App.tsx is now loaded with React.lazy; only Login and the two
layouts stay in the entry chunk. Shell wraps <Outlet> in a Suspense fallback
and a RouteErrorBoundary keyed on the path, and the root <Routes> gets the
same treatment, so a broken page renders a "Try again / Reload" card instead
of a blank screen.

Initial JS chunk drops from 1.79 MB to 379 kB (gzip 119 kB); ChatPanel
(367 kB) and recharts (373 kB) load only when their routes are visited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
